# Line-ending policy for the rlwm_trauma_analysis repo.
#
# Why: this repo is developed on Windows (CRLF default) and runs on M3
# Linux (LF default). Without an explicit policy, every text file
# round-trips between CRLF and LF, which (a) breaks bash shebangs on
# the cluster and (b) breaks Mutagen sync (which compares bytes, not
# git-normalized content, so every text file becomes a conflict).
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` means: git auto-detects text vs binary, and stores
# / checks out text files with LF universally. Binary files (PNGs,
# PDFs, .nc posteriors, etc.) pass through unchanged.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit LF for files where line endings affect behavior:
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.slurm text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.qmd   text eol=lf

# Explicit binary so they never get normalized
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.pdf   binary
*.nc    binary
*.npy   binary
*.npz   binary
*.parquet binary
*.feather binary
*.h5    binary
*.hdf5  binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.tar   binary
*.tgz   binary
